\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.18}{\ignorespaces Sketch of the amplitude stabilisation servo. The open loop transfer function was measured by injecting a signal into a $\times 1$ adding stage and measuring the ratio of the signal immediately after and just before this stage. \relax }}{74}{figure.caption.89}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchapteroltfmeasurement}{{3.18}{74}{Sketch of the amplitude stabilisation servo. The open loop transfer function was measured by injecting a signal into a $\times 1$ adding stage and measuring the ratio of the signal immediately after and just before this stage. \relax }{figure.caption.89}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{}{74}{section*.88}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.19}{\ignorespaces The open loop transfer function was measured using the layout shown in Figure \ref  {fig:ligolaserchapteroltfmeasurement}. The unity gain point is at 48\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\kilo \hertz } with 70\si {\degree } of phase margin. The shaping of the servo is $1/f$ at the unity gain point, but to achieve higher gain at low frequency, the servo has a $/f^3$ slope below the unity gain point. The measurement saturated below 100\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz. The model and measurement do not agree well below a few kHz due to the measurement saturating.\relax }}{75}{figure.caption.90}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchapteropenlooptransferfunction}{{3.19}{75}{The open loop transfer function was measured using the layout shown in Figure \ref {fig:ligolaserchapteroltfmeasurement}. The unity gain point is at 48\,\si {\kilo \hertz } with 70\si {\degree } of phase margin. The shaping of the servo is $1/f$ at the unity gain point, but to achieve higher gain at low frequency, the servo has a $/f^3$ slope below the unity gain point. The measurement saturated below 100\,Hz. The model and measurement do not agree well below a few kHz due to the measurement saturating.\relax }{figure.caption.90}{}}
