\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.26}{\ignorespaces The open loop transfer function was measured using the layout shown in Figure \ref  {fig:ligolaserchapterfrequencynoisemeasurementsketch}. This is shown in red. The transfer function of the electronics without the `boost' provided by an extra integrator stage was measured and is shown in blue. The model of this is shown in orange. The boosted electronics model is shown in purple. The green line shows the expected servo gain based on the boosted electronics model and the measurements shown in Figures \ref  {fig:ligolaserchaptermixercalibration} and \ref  {fig:ligolaserchapterpmcscan}. This model is within 2\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}dB of the measurement. The unity gain point was measured to be at $\sim 800$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz.\relax }}{89}{figure.caption.105}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchapterpmcloopmodeltf}{{3.26}{89}{The open loop transfer function was measured using the layout shown in Figure \ref {fig:ligolaserchapterfrequencynoisemeasurementsketch}. This is shown in red. The transfer function of the electronics without the `boost' provided by an extra integrator stage was measured and is shown in blue. The model of this is shown in orange. The boosted electronics model is shown in purple. The green line shows the expected servo gain based on the boosted electronics model and the measurements shown in Figures \ref {fig:ligolaserchaptermixercalibration} and \ref {fig:ligolaserchapterpmcscan}. This model is within 2\,dB of the measurement. The unity gain point was measured to be at $\sim 800$\,Hz.\relax }{figure.caption.105}{}}
