\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces The sensitivity curve for the A+ detectors expressed in units of $\si {\radian _{\rm  {rms}}/\sqrt  {Hz}}$. At frequencies above 1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}kHz the noise is flat ($3.4\times 10^{-5}\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\radian _{\rm  {rms}}/\sqrt  {\hertz }}$) as it is dominated by shot noise. At lower frequencies, the noise is increased relative to shot noise due to radiation pressure, coating thermal noise and other noise sources. At 5\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\hertz }, the noise is $8\times 10^{-5}\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\radian _{\rm  {rms}}/\sqrt  {\hertz }}$.\relax }}{145}{figure.caption.186}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterphasenoise}{{5.4}{145}{The sensitivity curve for the A+ detectors expressed in units of $\si {\radian _{\rm {rms}}/\sqrt {Hz}}$. At frequencies above 1\,kHz the noise is flat ($3.4\times 10^{-5}\,\si {\radian _{\rm {rms}}/\sqrt {\hertz }}$) as it is dominated by shot noise. At lower frequencies, the noise is increased relative to shot noise due to radiation pressure, coating thermal noise and other noise sources. At 5\,\si {\hertz }, the noise is $8\times 10^{-5}\,\si {\radian _{\rm {rms}}/\sqrt {\hertz }}$.\relax }{figure.caption.186}{}}
