\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.5}{\ignorespaces The sensitivity curve for A+ sets the limit on how much path length noise is acceptable between the AS and LO beams. The blue line shows sensitivity curve in units of path length noise between the AS and LO beams, and the orange line shows the longitudinal motion requirement for the optics which combine the LO and signal beam. At 5\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz, the longitudinal motion requirement for the optics is $4.9\times 10^{-13}\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\metre _{\rm  {rms}}/\sqrt  {\hertz }}$. The red line shows the level of shot noise; this is $2.1\times 10^{-17}\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\metre _{\rm  {rms}}/\sqrt  {\hertz }}$.\relax }}{147}{figure.caption.188}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterhrtsrequirement}{{5.5}{147}{The sensitivity curve for A+ sets the limit on how much path length noise is acceptable between the AS and LO beams. The blue line shows sensitivity curve in units of path length noise between the AS and LO beams, and the orange line shows the longitudinal motion requirement for the optics which combine the LO and signal beam. At 5\,Hz, the longitudinal motion requirement for the optics is $4.9\times 10^{-13}\,\si {\metre _{\rm {rms}}/\sqrt {\hertz }}$. The red line shows the level of shot noise; this is $2.1\times 10^{-17}\,\si {\metre _{\rm {rms}}/\sqrt {\hertz }}$.\relax }{figure.caption.188}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.6}{\ignorespaces A sketch of the LO and signal beam paths. The LO beam path is shown in blue, and the signal beam is shown in red. A dashed arrow indicates the direction that the recombining beam splitter, BHDBS2, may move in. If BHDBS2 moves in this way, the phase of the signal beam has increased while the phase of the LO beam has decreased at the point where the signal and LO beams combine. This means that the recombination beam splitter motion needs to be counted twice in calculations of the phase noise requirement.\relax }}{148}{figure.caption.189}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterbhddoublecounted}{{5.6}{148}{A sketch of the LO and signal beam paths. The LO beam path is shown in blue, and the signal beam is shown in red. A dashed arrow indicates the direction that the recombining beam splitter, BHDBS2, may move in. If BHDBS2 moves in this way, the phase of the signal beam has increased while the phase of the LO beam has decreased at the point where the signal and LO beams combine. This means that the recombination beam splitter motion needs to be counted twice in calculations of the phase noise requirement.\relax }{figure.caption.189}{}}
