\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {B.3}{\ignorespaces Circuit used to check that bias voltage noise was not contaminating dark noise measurements. To reach $5\si {\nano \volt /\sqrt  {\hertz }}$ at 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz, a 10V low noise reference IC (AD587JNZ) was used to generate the reverse bias. The output of this IC was filtered by two low pass filters (IC1A and IC2A). The transimpedance amplifier used is identical to the one shown in Figure \ref  {fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox1}\relax }}{249}{figure.caption.290}}
\newlabel{fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox2}{{B.3}{249}{Circuit used to check that bias voltage noise was not contaminating dark noise measurements. To reach $5\si {\nano \volt /\sqrt {\hertz }}$ at 10\,Hz, a 10V low noise reference IC (AD587JNZ) was used to generate the reverse bias. The output of this IC was filtered by two low pass filters (IC1A and IC2A). The transimpedance amplifier used is identical to the one shown in Figure \ref {fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox1}\relax }{figure.caption.290}{}}
