\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {B.4}{\ignorespaces The FD10D was biased with 1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}V in the circuits shown in Figure \ref  {fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox1} and Figure \ref  {fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox3}. The low noise fixed bias circuit and the circuit with a settable bias gave the same results, so we can be confident that the circuits shown in Figures \ref  {fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox1} and \ref  {fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox2} will produce measurements that are not contaminated by bias noise.\relax }}{250}{figure.caption.291}}
\newlabel{fig:pdchapterbiascrosscheck}{{B.4}{250}{The FD10D was biased with 1\,V in the circuits shown in Figure \ref {fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox1} and Figure \ref {fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox3}. The low noise fixed bias circuit and the circuit with a settable bias gave the same results, so we can be confident that the circuits shown in Figures \ref {fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox1} and \ref {fig:circuitappendixdarknoisetestbox2} will produce measurements that are not contaminated by bias noise.\relax }{figure.caption.291}{}}
